{"key":"ctet","title":"CTET (Teacher Eligibility Test)","kind":"Teaching","blurb":"CTET preparation in 7 modules and 52 chapters.","modules":[{"number":1,"title":"Child Development & Pedagogy","summary":"Compulsory in both papers — 30 marks, 20% of the whole exam. The single highest-yield section: learning theories (Piaget, Vygotsky, Kohlberg), intelligence, inclusive education, motivation and assessment. Authored once and shared by Paper I and Paper II (only the age focus differs).","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"growth-and-development","title":"Development & Its Relationship with Learning","topics":["Growth vs Development","Principles of Development","Heredity & Environment","Socialization & Agents","Development and Learning"]},{"number":2,"slug":"piaget-cognitive-development","title":"Piaget's Theory of Cognitive Development","topics":["Schema, Assimilation & Accommodation","Sensorimotor Stage","Preoperational Stage","Concrete Operational Stage","Formal Operational Stage","Classroom Implications & Critique"]},{"number":3,"slug":"vygotsky-social-constructivism","title":"Vygotsky's Social Constructivism","topics":["Social Construction of Knowledge","Zone of Proximal Development (ZPD)","Scaffolding","Role of Language & Culture","Piaget vs Vygotsky"]},{"number":4,"slug":"kohlberg-moral-development","title":"Kohlberg's Stages of Moral Development","topics":["Pre-conventional Level","Conventional Level","Post-conventional Level","The Heinz Dilemma","Critique & Classroom Use"]},{"number":5,"slug":"theories-of-intelligence","title":"Intelligence & Its Multi-Dimensional View","topics":["Concept & Critique of IQ","Gardner's Multiple Intelligences","Spearman, Thurstone & Guilford","Sternberg's Triarchic Theory","Implications for Teaching"]},{"number":6,"slug":"language-thought-and-difference","title":"Language, Thought & Individual Differences","topics":["Language & Thought","Gender as a Social Construct","Individual Differences among Learners","Diversity: Language, Caste, Religion, Community"]},{"number":7,"slug":"inclusive-education","title":"Inclusive Education & Children with Special Needs","topics":["Concept of Inclusive Education","Disadvantaged & Deprived Learners","Learning Difficulties (Dyslexia, Dyscalculia)","Sensory & Physical Impairments","Gifted, Creative & Talented Learners"]},{"number":8,"slug":"learning-and-motivation","title":"How Children Learn & Motivation","topics":["Behaviourism, Cognitivism & Constructivism","How & Why Children Learn","Children's Errors & Alternative Conceptions","Cognition & Emotions","Motivation: Intrinsic & Extrinsic","Factors Affecting Learning"]},{"number":9,"slug":"assessment-and-evaluation","title":"Assessment, Evaluation & CCE","topics":["Assessment FOR vs OF Learning","Continuous & Comprehensive Evaluation","School-Based Assessment","Formulating Appropriate Questions"]}]},{"number":2,"title":"Language I — English","summary":"Comprehension (two unseen passages — prose and poem), a dedicated CTET Grammar & Verbal Ability bank, plus the Pedagogy of Language Development. All three are authored for CTET and shared across both papers.","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"english-reading-comprehension","title":"Reading Comprehension (Prose, Poem & Drama)","topics":["Main Idea & Detail","Inference & Tone","Vocabulary in Context","Poetic Devices & Figures of Speech"]},{"number":2,"slug":"english-grammar","title":"Grammar & Verbal Ability","topics":["Tenses","Parts of Speech","Articles & Prepositions","Active/Passive Voice & Narration","Subject-Verb Agreement","Synonyms, Antonyms & Word Formation"]},{"number":3,"slug":"pedagogy-of-language-development","title":"Pedagogy of Language Development","topics":["Learning vs Acquisition","Principles & Methods of Language Teaching","Listening, Speaking, Reading, Writing (LSRW)","Role of Grammar — A Critical View","Language in a Diverse Classroom","Evaluation & Remedial Teaching","Teaching–Learning Materials"]}]},{"number":3,"title":"भाषा II — हिन्दी","summary":"अपठित बोध (दो अपठित गद्यांश), व्याकरण और भाषा विकास का अध्यापन। हिन्दी व्याकरण व शिक्षण-शास्त्र दोनों पेपरों के लिए नए सिरे से तैयार — GrowQR पर पहली बार।","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"hindi-vyakaran","title":"हिन्दी व्याकरण (संज्ञा, सर्वनाम, संधि, समास)","topics":["संज्ञा, सर्वनाम, विशेषण, क्रिया","काल एवं वाच्य","संधि एवं समास","उपसर्ग एवं प्रत्यय"]},{"number":2,"slug":"hindi-shabd-gyan","title":"शब्द-ज्ञान एवं अपठित बोध","topics":["पर्यायवाची एवं विलोम","मुहावरे एवं लोकोक्तियाँ","अनेकार्थी एवं वाक्यांश के लिए एक शब्द","अपठित गद्यांश"]},{"number":3,"slug":"hindi-bhasha-shikshan","title":"भाषा विकास का अध्यापन (शिक्षण-शास्त्र)","topics":["अधिगम और अर्जन","भाषा शिक्षण के सिद्धांत","भाषा कौशल (LSRW)","विविध कक्षा की चुनौतियाँ","मूल्यांकन एवं उपचारात्मक शिक्षण"]}]},{"number":4,"title":"Mathematics & Its Pedagogy","summary":"Content plus the Pedagogy of Mathematics. The Primary (Class I–V) content is a full, competition-level Maths bank authored for CTET — 14 chapters across geometry, numbers, the four operations, measurement, data and money, with thousands of pedagogy-rich MCQs. The Elementary (VI–VIII) content reuses GrowQR’s existing course; the maths-pedagogy block is shared by both papers.","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"maths-pedagogy","title":"Pedagogy of Mathematics","topics":["Nature of Mathematics & Logical Thinking","Place of Maths in the Curriculum","Language of Mathematics","Community Mathematics","Error Analysis & Diagnostic Teaching","Evaluation & Problems of Teaching"]},{"number":2,"slug":"maths-basic-geometry","title":"Basic Geometry — Shapes & Symmetry","topics":["Plane Shapes (2-D Shapes)","Properties of Shapes","Geometrical Concepts","Symmetry"]},{"number":3,"slug":"maths-shapes-spatial","title":"Shapes & Spatial Understanding","topics":["Spatial Vocabulary","Direction Sense","Visualisation Skills","2-D and 3-D Recognition"]},{"number":4,"slug":"maths-solids","title":"Solids Around Us (3-D Shapes)","topics":["Identification of Solids","Properties of Solids","Real-Life Examples","Sorting and Classification"]},{"number":5,"slug":"maths-numbers","title":"Numbers & the Number System","topics":["Counting","Number Names","Place Value","Expanded Form","Comparison of Numbers","Ordering Numbers","Number Patterns","Odd and Even Numbers","Roman Numerals (Basic)"]},{"number":6,"slug":"maths-addition-subtraction","title":"Addition & Subtraction","topics":["Addition","Subtraction","Mental Mathematics","Word Problems","Estimation"]},{"number":7,"slug":"maths-multiplication","title":"Multiplication","topics":["Multiplication Facts","Properties","Multiplication Algorithms","Word Problems"]},{"number":8,"slug":"maths-division","title":"Division","topics":["Equal Sharing","Equal Grouping","Division Facts","Quotient and Remainder","Long Division (Elementary Level)","Word Problems"]},{"number":9,"slug":"maths-measurement","title":"Measurement (Length)","topics":["Non-Standard Units","Standard Units","Conversion of Units","Perimeter (Basic Introduction)","Estimation of Length"]},{"number":10,"slug":"maths-weight","title":"Weight (Mass)","topics":["Heavy and Light","Standard Units","Unit Conversions","Practical Weight Measurement","Word Problems"]},{"number":11,"slug":"maths-time","title":"Time — Clock & Calendar","topics":["Reading Clock","Time Formats","Units of Time","Calendar","Elapsed Time","Word Problems"]},{"number":12,"slug":"maths-volume","title":"Volume (Capacity)","topics":["Concepts","Units","Unit Conversion","Estimation","Practical Applications"]},{"number":13,"slug":"maths-data-handling","title":"Data Handling","topics":["Data Collection","Data Organization","Tables","Tally Marks","Pictographs","Bar Graphs (Elementary)","Reading Data","Drawing Conclusions"]},{"number":14,"slug":"maths-patterns","title":"Patterns","topics":["Number Patterns","Shape Patterns","Pattern Rules","Missing Elements"]},{"number":15,"slug":"maths-money","title":"Money","topics":["Indian Currency","Reading Currency Values","Addition and Subtraction of Money","Making Bills","Profit and Cost (Elementary Understanding)","Shopping-Based Problems","Change and Balance"]},{"number":16,"slug":"maths2-number-system","title":"Number System (Classes VI–VIII)","topics":["Knowing Our Numbers & Estimation","Playing with Numbers (Factors, Multiples, HCF, LCM)","Integers & Their Operations","Fractions & Decimals","Rational Numbers","Squares, Cubes & Exponents"]},{"number":17,"slug":"maths2-algebra","title":"Algebra (Classes VI–VIII)","topics":["Algebraic Expressions","Linear Equations in One Variable","Exponents & Powers","Algebraic Identities & Factorisation"]},{"number":18,"slug":"maths2-ratio-proportion","title":"Ratio, Proportion & Commercial Maths (VI–VIII)","topics":["Ratio, Proportion & Unitary Method","Percentage","Profit, Loss & Discount","Simple Interest","Direct & Inverse Proportion"]},{"number":19,"slug":"maths2-geometry","title":"Geometry (Classes VI–VIII)","topics":["Basic Geometrical Ideas","Lines & Angles","Triangles & Their Properties","Quadrilaterals & Polygons","Congruence & Symmetry","Practical Geometry (Construction)"]},{"number":20,"slug":"maths2-mensuration","title":"Mensuration (Classes VI–VIII)","topics":["Perimeter & Area of Plane Figures","Area of Triangles, Parallelograms & Circles","Surface Area & Volume of Solids"]},{"number":21,"slug":"maths2-data-probability","title":"Data Handling & Probability (VI–VIII)","topics":["Organising & Representing Data","Bar Graphs, Pie Charts & Histograms","Mean, Median & Mode","Introduction to Probability"]}]},{"number":5,"title":"Environmental Studies (EVS)","summary":"Paper I only. Six NCERT themes — Family & Friends, Food, Shelter, Water, Travel, Things We Make & Do — plus the pedagogy of EVS. New to GrowQR, authored here.","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"evs-family-and-friends","title":"Family & Friends (Relationships, Work, Animals, Plants)","topics":["Relationships & Community","Work and Play","Animals: Habitats & Care","Plants: Parts, Uses & Growth"]},{"number":2,"slug":"evs-food-shelter-water","title":"Food, Shelter & Water","topics":["Food: Sources, Cooking & Preservation","Shelter: Houses & Materials","Water: Sources, Uses & Conservation"]},{"number":3,"slug":"evs-travel-and-things-we-do","title":"Travel & Things We Make and Do","topics":["Means of Transport & Journeys","Maps & Directions","Crafts, Tools & Materials"]},{"number":4,"slug":"evs-pedagogy","title":"Pedagogy of Environmental Studies","topics":["Concept & Scope of EVS","EVS as a Bridge: Science & Social Science","Activities, Experimentation & Discussion","CCE & Teaching Aids in EVS"]}]},{"number":6,"title":"Science & Its Pedagogy","summary":"Paper II (Maths & Science option). A full, CTET-native Science bank across the seven NCERT themes — Food, Materials, The World of the Living, Moving Things, How Things Work, Natural Phenomena and Natural Resources — plus the pedagogy of science. Authored for CTET, not reused.","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"science-pedagogy","title":"Pedagogy of Science","topics":["Nature & Structure of Science","Aims & Objectives of Teaching Science","Approaches: Observation, Experiment, Discovery","Innovation & Teaching Aids","Evaluation & Remedial Teaching"]},{"number":2,"slug":"science2-food","title":"Food (Classes VI–VIII)","topics":["Components of Food & Nutrients","Sources of Food: Plants & Animals","Balanced Diet & Deficiency Diseases","Food Spoilage & Preservation"]},{"number":3,"slug":"science2-materials","title":"Materials (Classes VI–VIII)","topics":["Materials of Daily Use & Their Properties","Separation of Substances","Metals & Non-Metals","Acids, Bases & Salts","Physical & Chemical Changes"]},{"number":4,"slug":"science2-living-world","title":"The World of the Living (VI–VIII)","topics":["Plants: Structure & Functions","Animals: Nutrition & Body Systems","Cell & Microorganisms","Reproduction in Living Things","Ecosystem, Health & Nutrition"]},{"number":5,"slug":"science2-moving-things","title":"Moving Things, People & Ideas (VI–VIII)","topics":["Motion, Distance & Time","Force & Pressure","Friction"]},{"number":6,"slug":"science2-how-things-work","title":"How Things Work — Electricity & Magnets (VI–VIII)","topics":["Electric Current & Circuits","Conductors, Insulators & Effects of Current","Magnets & Their Properties"]},{"number":7,"slug":"science2-natural-phenomena","title":"Natural Phenomena — Light, Sound & Heat (VI–VIII)","topics":["Light & Reflection","Sound","Heat & Temperature","Rain, Thunder, Lightning & Earthquakes"]},{"number":8,"slug":"science2-natural-resources","title":"Natural Resources (VI–VIII)","topics":["Air, Water & Soil","Conservation & Pollution","Coal, Petroleum & Sources of Energy"]}]},{"number":7,"title":"Social Studies & Its Pedagogy","summary":"Paper II (Social Studies option) — 60 Q. History, Geography and Social & Political Life (Civics) plus the pedagogy of social science. New to GrowQR, authored here.","chapters":[{"number":1,"slug":"social-history","title":"History — Our Pasts (Ancient to Modern India)","topics":["Sources & Earliest Societies","First Cities & Early Empires","Sultans, Mughals & Regional Cultures","Company Rule & The Revolt of 1857","Nationalist Movement & After Independence"]},{"number":2,"slug":"social-geography","title":"Geography — Earth, Environment & Resources","topics":["Planet Earth & the Globe","Air, Water & Natural Environment","Human Environment & Settlement","Resources & Agriculture"]},{"number":3,"slug":"social-civics","title":"Social & Political Life (Civics)","topics":["Diversity & Government","Local & State Government","Democracy & The Constitution","Parliament, Judiciary & Social Justice"]},{"number":4,"slug":"social-pedagogy","title":"Pedagogy of Social Science","topics":["Concept & Nature of Social Science","Critical Thinking & Inquiry","Primary & Secondary Sources","Project Work & Evaluation"]}]}]}